.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-ROTATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-rotate - Rotate personal ENV scope keys while preserving values


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env rotate [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Rotate personal ENV scope keys while preserving values

.PP
Rotate personal ENV scope keys while retaining the values. Complete or cancel an interrupted rotation before starting another custody change.

.PP
ENV values are encrypted before they leave the client. Commands select personal, team, or host scope explicitly; list output shows metadata rather than secret values. Unlock the local vault when a key operation requires it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rotate

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP, \fBpb-env-rotate-cancel(1)\fP
